<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.organizations.billing.getOrganizationPaymentMethod({
  path: {
    organizationId: "organizationId",
  },
});
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon
from photon_api.rpc_generated import GetOrganizationPaymentMethodInput

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.organizations.billing.get_organization_payment_method(
    GetOrganizationPaymentMethodInput.model_validate({
        "path": {
            "organizationId": "organizationId",
        },
    })
)
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .get_organization_payment_method("organizationId".to_owned())
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

<ResponseExample>
```json 200
{
  "cardOnFile": true,
  "paymentMethod": null
}
```

</ResponseExample>

## Parameters

<ParamField path="organizationId" type={"string"} required>

</ParamField>


## Returns

**`200`** Whether the organization has a captured card and its metadata. GetOrganizationPaymentMethodResponse

<ResponseField name="cardOnFile" type={"boolean"} required>
True once a card is captured for the payer.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="paymentMethod" type={"PaymentMethod | null"} required>
Metadata for the default card, or null.
</ResponseField>

